How can agronomist overcome problems due to persistent use of fertilizers?
Agronomists are faced with the problem of persistent use of fertilizers, which leads to a decrease in soil fertility and an increase in the cost of production. The main cause of this is the fact that the fertilizer is applied too frequently, and the soil is not sufficiently replenished with nutrients.
The most common causes of fertilizer overuse are:
• Incorrect application of fertilizers;
• Inappropriate choice of fertilizers;
• Insufficient soil preparation;
• Inadequate soil moisture;
• Insufficient soil temperature
